<h3 id="projects">PROJECTS</h3>
<p><strong>Radio Differences of Broad Absorption Line Quasars</strong> - LOFAR DR2 - Durham University <span style="float: right; ">2020-Present</span><br />
What drives the radio differences between sources with very similar properties across the rest of the spectrum? Broad Absorption Line Quasars show fast moving outflows that are thought to be a prime mode of AGN feedback which can modify the behaviour of a galaxy hosting a supermassive blackhole. However, the two main varieties of BALs show significantly different radio properties that are yet to be explained. Using international LOFAR data I will place these sources more accurately both in an evolutionary timeline and in a cohesive model that can explain them.</p>

